  "narrative": {
    "intro": "V2X Aerospace has $1.3B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. V2X Aerospace won 83 awards so far in the fiscal year. V2X Aerospace shows an average award size of $15.5M and obligations fell 16.4% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $960M in FY2026 to date, followed by the General Services Administration with $287M and the Department of Justice with $26.3M. Other buyers in FY2026 to date include the Department of Homeland Security with $10.4M and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $2.7M. Other Support Activities for Air Transportation is V2X Aerospace’s largest market at $886M, followed by Engineering Services at $328M and Aircraft Manufacturing at $33.7M. V2X Aerospace records smaller totals in Other Scientific and Technical Consulting Services at $20.1M, All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $18.3M, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $500. Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing and Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing show $0.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are V2X Aerospace’s federal obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $960M in FY2026 to date. V2X Aerospace’s top market, Other Support Activities for Air Transportation, accounts for $886M of obligations. The next largest market is Engineering Services at $328M, showing a clear concentration in aviation and engineering work. Smaller markets include Aircraft Manufacturing at $33.7M and several categories with single-digit millions or zero."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How has V2X Aerospace’s yearly obligation profile trended recently?",
        "body": "Annual obligations rose from $958M in FY21 to $1.5B in FY25 before falling to $1.3B in FY26 to date. Obligations fell 16.4% year over year. The FY26 to date total is partial for the fiscal year. Past years show the sequence $958M, $1.1B, $1B, $1.2B, $1.5B, $1.3B."
      }
    ]
