  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does V2X Aerospace make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "V2X Aerospace makes $1.3B from federal contracts in FY2026 to date. V2X Aerospace received 83 awards so far this fiscal year and the average award size is $15.5M. The current-year total is a fiscal year to date number and therefore partial."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from V2X Aerospace?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense is V2X Aerospace’s largest buyer, obligating $960M in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration obligated $287M, the Department of Justice obligated $26.3M, the Department of Homeland Security obligated $10.4M, and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $2.7M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does V2X Aerospace sell to the government?",
      "a": "V2X Aerospace sells primarily aviation and engineering services to the government, with Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $886M and Engineering Services at $328M. V2X Aerospace also has obligations in Aircraft Manufacturing at $33.7M, Other Scientific and Technical Consulting Services at $20.1M, All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $18.3M, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $500; two categories show $0."
